no-browser: rhythm echo: no Chrome or Chromium found; install Chrome, pass --browser /path/to/chrome, or allow the one-time Chrome for Testing download
sandbox-root: rhythm echo: Chrome won't start without its sandbox as root; run as another user, or pass --no-sandbox (only for sites you trust)
unreachable: rhythm echo: https://staging.shop.test/ didn't answer: dial tcp 127.0.0.1:443: connection refused. Is the site running? A local site with a self-signed certificate needs -k
unreachable: rhythm echo: https://staging.shop.test/ didn't answer: dial tcp: lookup staging.shop.test: no such host. Is the site running? A local site with a self-signed certificate needs -k
http-status: rhythm echo: https://staging.shop.test/ answered 401 Unauthorized; pass the login with -H "Authorization: env:RHYTHM_ECHO_STAGING_AUTH" or consent: headers:
http-status: rhythm echo: https://staging.shop.test/ answered 503 Service Unavailable; check that the site serves its pages, then run the check again
bot-wall: rhythm echo: https://shop.example.com/ showed a bot check (Cloudflare) instead of the page; allow this machine in the firewall for the check, or check staging
bot-wall: rhythm echo: https://shop.example.com/ showed a bot check instead of the page; allow this machine in the firewall for the check, or check staging
redirect-host: rhythm echo: https://shop.test/ redirects to https://shop.example.com/; check that one, or pass --follow-host
tls: rhythm echo: https://shop.example/ uses a certificate this machine doesn't trust (x509: certificate signed by unknown authority); pass -k for a local or private site
no-browser-image: rhythm echo: this image has no browser; run rhythm echo consent on the host, or pass --browser
redirect-loop: rhythm echo: https://shop.test/ redirects in a loop or through more than 10 hops; check the site's redirects
write: rhythm echo: couldn't write .echo/consent/x/events/page-1-none.ndjson: no space left on device
something-new: rhythm echo: consent: something-new: https://shop.test/: what happened
no-browser in the image: rhythm echo: this image has no browser; run rhythm echo consent on the host, or pass --browser
